  [premise-corrected: a registry release carries all but one of them — crates.io `taffy` 0.15.1 (2026-10-25, MSRV 1.71, the same dependency list as 0.15.0) holds 13 of the 14 Taffy commits the four bring, by subject against `v0.15.0...ea07c4c3`. The one it lacks is #1303, the caller-defined float id, which `v0.15.1`'s commit `93db25f7` drops from 0.15.x. `1a11761bc`'s one `inline.rs` line exists only for #1303. So the take moves the lock to 0.15.1 (`cargo update -p taffy --precise 0.15.1`, 2 lock lines, `Cargo.toml` unchanged), and #1303 with its `inline.rs` line stays out. Measured both ways (research §The Taffy carry): the git take picks clean, 3 files +3 −3, every leg green, so the master rule alone stops it. The founder question covers #1303 and the later git-Taffy chain only.]

